WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.137
This query trims name boundaries, collapses repeated whitespace, and applies title-style capitalization.

00:00:07.137 --> 00:00:10.382
Run it and compare raw and cleaned names.

00:00:10.382 --> 00:00:14.742
The goal is to create a more consistent analytical representation.

00:00:14.742 --> 00:00:21.542
In production, name capitalization can be domain-sensitive, so treat INITCAP as a teaching convenience rather

00:00:21.542 --> 00:00:29.092
than a universal truth. Standardization should make equivalent values comparable without inventing facts.

00:00:29.092 --> 00:00:36.982
Lowercasing an email or normalizing a known category map is different from guessing what an ambiguous value

00:00:36.982 --> 00:00:41.947
was supposed to mean. Good cleaning reduces representation noise while preserving uncertainty.
